> ### Abilities to remember
> 
> **Goblins — Nimble Escape.** Each goblin can take the **Disengage** or **Hide** action as a bonus action. Have them shoot from cover, then duck behind trees, rocks, or the creek bank.
> 
> **Wolves — Pack Tactics.** A wolf has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the wolf’s allies is within 5 feet of that creature and not incapacitated.
> 
> ### Encounter difficulty note
> 
> Against four PCs at levels 3–5, these standard creatures are a relatively easy encounter if fought in the open. To make it feel like a real ambush without making the stat blocks deadlier:
> 
> - Begin with goblins in half cover behind rocks, fallen logs, or the far creek bank.
> - Have one wolf attempt to knock Ekemon or Varkash prone while the other and nearby goblins exploit the opening.
> - Put two goblins on elevated ground or in trees.
> - Include the snare trap described earlier.
> - Have the goblins retreat once three or four have fallen, unless their whistle alarm has sounded.
